{
  "id": 529706525,
  "iid": 26433,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "OpenFlow v4: Validate hello element length to prevent exception",
  "description": "Summary:\n\nIn dissect_openflow_hello_element_v4(), elem_length was used without validating that it is at least 4 bytes (the minimum size of a type + length header). When elem_length was less than 4, (elem_length - 4) resulted in negative lengths passed to proto_tree_add_item(), throwing a dissector exception and aborting dissection.\n\nChanges:\n\n\\- Added a validation check ensuring elem_length is at least 4 bytes before dissecting the element body.\n\n\\- Verified with tools/check_apis.py (0 warnings).",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2026-09-09T03:13:32.207Z",
