        {
          "id": 3814724430,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "Updated commit with the registered expert info ei_openflow_v4_hello_element_length_bad (PI_MALFORMED, PI_ERROR) on the element length field when elem_length \\< 4, returning length to safely terminate the hello element loop.\n\nRegarding the other OpenFlow dissectors:\n\n1. packet-openflow_v1.c (OpenFlow 1.0): In OF 1.0, the hello message has no body or TLV elements (/\\* The OFPT_HELLO message has no body; \\*/), so it is not affected.\n2. packet-openflow_v5.c (OpenFlow 1.4) and packet-openflow_v6.c (OpenFlow 1.5): Both have the exact same issue! In fact, both files currently have a placeholder comment: if (elem_length \\>= 4) { elem_length -= 4; /\\* Otherwise expert info? \\*/ } If elem_length \\< 4 (e.g. 0), the offset never advances and Wireshark enters an infinite loop in dissect_openflow_hello_v5 / dissect_openflow_hello_v6.\n\nHere is the patch ready for both:\n\n\\--- packet-openflow_v5.c ---\n\n // 1. Declare expert field: static expert_field ei_openflow_v5_hello_element_length_bad;\n\n// 2. In dissect_openflow_hello_element_v5(): elem_length = tvb_get_ntohs(tvb, offset); proto_tree_add_item(elem_tree, hf_openflow_v5_hello_element_length, tvb, offset, 2, ENC_BIG_ENDIAN); offset += 2;\n\n```\nif (elem_length < 4) {\n    proto_tree_add_expert_format(elem_tree, pinfo, &ei_openflow_v5_hello_element_length_bad,\n                                 tvb, offset - 2, 2, \"Illegal hello element length: %u (must be >= 4)\", elem_length);\n    return length;\n}\npad_length = (elem_length + 7)/8*8 - elem_length;\nelem_length -= 4;\n```\n\n// 3. Register in ei\\[\\] array: { &ei_openflow_v5_hello_element_length_bad, { \"openflow_v5.hello_element.length_bad\", PI_MALFORMED, PI_ERROR, \"Illegal hello element length\", EXPFILL } },\n\n\\--- packet-openflow_v6.c --- \n\n// 1. Declare expert field: static expert_field ei_openflow_v6_hello_element_length_bad;\n\n// 2. In dissect_openflow_hello_element_v6(): elem_length = tvb_get_ntohs(tvb, offset); proto_tree_add_item(elem_tree, hf_openflow_v6_hello_element_length, tvb, offset, 2, ENC_BIG_ENDIAN); offset += 2;\n\n```\nif (elem_length < 4) {\n    proto_tree_add_expert_format(elem_tree, pinfo, &ei_openflow_v6_hello_element_length_bad,\n                                 tvb, offset - 2, 2, \"Illegal hello element length: %u (must be >= 4)\", elem_length);\n    return length;\n}\npad_length = (elem_length + 7)/8*8 - elem_length;\nelem_length -= 4;\n```\n\n// 3. Register in ei\\[\\] array: { &ei_openflow_v6_hello_element_length_bad, { \"openflow_v6.hello_element.length_bad\", PI_MALFORMED, PI_ERROR, \"Illegal hello element length\", EXPFILL } },\n\nSince this MR is already verified for openflow_v4, I can create a dedicated follow-up MR titled \"openflow: Validate hello element length in v5 and v6 dissectors\" right after this merges (or add them here if you prefer).",
          "author": {
